# A starter suite: a coin-operated turnstile. Check it, then make it yours:
#
#   expectation check <this directory>
#
# The language: https://expectation.sim001.net/guide/language.html

Suite: Turnstile

Vocabulary:
  # The states the system can be in and the events that can happen. Every step below uses
  # these words, so a step outside them is an error.
  State: the turnstile is locked | unlocked
  State: the coin box has 0..1000 coins
  Event: a visitor inserts a coin
    # How the manual tells a reader to do it:
    Say: put a coin in the slot
  Event: a visitor pushes the arm
    Say: push the arm

Background:
  # Where every test starts.
  Given the turnstile is locked
  And the coin box has 0 coins

Feature: Paying to go through
  # Text before the first expectation is the feature's page in the manual.
  The turnstile lets one visitor through for each coin.

  Expectation: A coin unlocks it
    Given the turnstile is locked
    When a visitor inserts a coin
    Then the turnstile is unlocked
    And the coin box goes up by 1

  Expectation: Pushing through locks it again
    Given the turnstile is unlocked
    When a visitor pushes the arm
    Then the turnstile is locked

  Expectation: Pushing a locked turnstile does nothing
    Given the turnstile is locked
    When a visitor pushes the arm
    Then the turnstile is locked

# A story is a journey through the expectations. It becomes a tutorial and an acceptance test;
# the expectations it passes through supply the checks.
Story: A day at the zoo
  As a visitor
  I want to pay once and go through
  So that I can see the animals

  When a visitor pushes the arm
  Then the turnstile is locked
  When a visitor inserts a coin
  Then the turnstile is unlocked
  When a visitor pushes the arm
  Then the turnstile is locked
